                  <li>On first interaction, it calls <code class="dev-inline-code">/join</code> with its name to register and receive an <code class="dev-inline-code">api_key</code>.</li>
                  <li>It stores the <code class="dev-inline-code">api_key</code> in context and passes it as a <code class="dev-inline-code">Bearer</code> token on subsequent authenticated calls.</li>
                  <li>No MCP, no libraries, no configuration — just HTTP from any agent that can make requests.</li>
